 (each section is an explicit field)","Plan Scope lists only `_config_schema.py` dataclass + `_config_sections.py` _SECTIONS registration"],"finding":"The plan asserts warnings.cross_session reads 'through the composed Config (the same load path every other typed key uses)', but Config.from_mapping (src/rebar/_config_schema.py:703) instantiates each section via _SECTION_CLASSES[sect](**vals) and constructs cls(**{sect: ...}); a new section therefore also requires an entry in _SECTION_CLASSES (line 707) AND a field on the Config dataclass (lines 680-693). The plan's scope names only _SECTIONS registration + the dataclass definition, omitting _SECTION_CLASSES and the Config field. With only _SECTIONS wired, coercion succeeds but cls(warnings=...) raises TypeError, so the asserted load path cannot resolve the key.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0422978682080ce9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — 'Read it through the composed Config (the same load path every other typed key uses)'","norm_id":"n4f2028cbccb1b82e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Loading a rebar.toml with [warnings] cross_session=false through Config.from_mapping","The AC test_cross_session_config_toggle constructing a Config from a mapping"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Scope for src/rebar/_config_schema.py, add: (1) a `WarningsConfig` dataclass with `cross_session: bool = _documented(True, ...)`, (2) a `warnings: WarningsConfig = field(default_factory=WarningsConfig)` field on `Config`, and (3) a `\"warnings\": WarningsConfig` entry in `_SECTION_CLASSES`, alongside the existing `_SECTIONS` registration.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_fi